                                "sense_id": "0c042dc6-f64c-365d-8890-44f6198fbffa",
                                "text": "Claius presently went to a Fisherman, & having agreed with him, and provided some apparrell for the naked stranger, he imbarked, and the Shepheards with him: and were no sooner gone beyond the mouth of the haven, but that some way into the sea they might discerne (as it were) a stayne of the waters colour, and by times some sparkes and smoke mounting thereout."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2918e4eb-4a1e-4b37-984e-fa7141425e2e",
                                "sense_id": "0c042dc6-f64c-365d-8890-44f6198fbffa",
                                "text": "Thereout a strange beast with seven heads arose, / That townes and castles under her brest did coure."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dfbe4792-142d-4f02-889a-c6b0dab73f28",
                                "sense_id": "0c042dc6-f64c-365d-8890-44f6198fbffa",
                                "text": "\"Keep thy money, man, and gi's thy hand,\" says he, and they shake hands; but the old gamester gives the new hat to the shepherd, and, soon after, the half-sovereign to Willum, who thereout decorates his sweetheart with ribbons to his heart's content."
                            }
